(text "XEM JTAG TARGET" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 576.16 545.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top)) (uuid "28095679-d1aa-477d-819c-e7508a1938eb"))
(rectangle (start 1073 280) (end 1288 445) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "08695f15-fd16-4d39-b2cc-bb859b4f3775"))
(text "Function: J500 and U501 convert USB-C to JTAG; U505 stores the programmer settings.\nU602 translates the JTAG lines to 1.8 V. SW600 selects the XEM or one of eight frontends.\nU603 checks the selected target voltage; U605 enables the translator after a delay.\nC601/C603 bypass the XEM rails; U610 selects the XEM path. Turn OFF before selecting." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1077 284 0) (effects (font (size 1.55 1.55)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b39bcb74-bfbb-4c36-967c-328eeb566ab7"))
(text "Source / changes: USB-C input: Codex adaptation of BRK8305 A03,\n25Oct2023, JTAG sheet8/PDFp4: https://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nJ500=USB4110-GF-A; D500=USBLC6-2SC6. C506\nchanged 10nF to 100nF. USB shell uses C502/FB503;\nshared DGND. Connector fit and USB/ESD layout unverified.\nST USBLC6-2 Rev7 Fig15: https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/usblc6-2.pdf\n\nFT232H and EEPROM: Codex adaptation of BRK8305 A03,\n25Oct2023, JTAG sheet8/PDFp4: https://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nFT232HQ pins13/14/15/16=TCK/TDI/TDO/TMS; ADBUS4-7\nand ACBUS NC as BRK8305. Former R508 removed.\nU505=93LC56BT-I/SN (SOIC) replaces CFG001/MSOP;\nY500=SJK replaces Abracon; FB500–502=Murata BLM18AG601SN1D.\nY500 specifies 18pF load; 18pF C503/C504 give ~9pF + stray.\nConfirm crystal load, frequency, drive and startup after layout.\nY500: https://xonstorage.z8.web.core.windows.net/pdf/sjk_7u12000e18ucg_xonjuly20_20_link.pdf\nBead current and voltage drop need checks.\nMicrochip DS21794F Table3-1: https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/en/DeviceDoc/21794F.pdf\nFT232H DS v2.2 sec3,6: https://ftdichip.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DS_FT232H.pdf\nAMD program_ftdi EEPROM write/readback and Vivado\nenumeration must be tested. VCK190 match not established.\nhttps://docs.amd.com/r/2024.1-English/ug908-vivado-programming-debugging/Programming-FTDI-Devices-for-Vivado-Hardware-Manager-Support\n\nTranslator: Codex adaptation; TI TXU0304 Rev A sec.9: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/txu0304.pdf\nVCCA = FTDI3V3; VCCB = XEM +1.8 V (MC1.2); R601–R603 = 22R provisional.\nR604 pull-up removed; IC inputs have weak pulldowns. Check rail sequencing, unpowered-target\ninjection, timing, cable loading and FTDI/Vivado operation.\n\nRail bypass: Codex adaptation: C601/C603 retained from the removed regulators.\nXEM8310 MC2.70 = +3.3 V and MC1.2 = +1.8 V; rail budget and startup must be verified.\nOpal Kelly XEM8310 pin list: https://pins.opalkelly.com/pin_list/XEM8310\n\nRotary selector: Codex direct-to-enable wiring; nine 10k pulls replace decoder logic.\nALPS SRBQ 1P9T non-shorting; confirm stock, contact sequence and footprint.\nhttps://tech.alpsalpine.com/e/products/detail/SRBQ490100/\nBounce and switch faults are not proven.\n\nOFF/ENABLE: Codex dual-pole arrangement; R600 biases MASTER low.\nC&K JS datasheet p.9; verify contact positions and footprint:\nhttps://www.littelfuse.com/assetdocs/littelfuse-c-k-slide-js-series-datasheet?assetguid=aba42b08-0d2c-423b-813d-a2faa5a3bb14\n\nVoltage window: Codex circuit; TI TPS3700 Rev G sec.7.3: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps3700.pdf\nXEM 3.3 V supplies U603. Selected VREF uses XEM R629 or HDMI pin 1.\nR605–R608=301k/100k and 402k/100k; R613/C608 discharge/filter.\nNominal window 1.604–2.008 V; verify leakage, tolerance and startup.\n\nDelay: Codex circuit; TI TPS3808 Rev N secs.4, 7: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps3808.pdf\nU605 changed G33 to G30: 2.79 V nominal threshold increases 3.3 V rail margin.\nCT open: nominal 20 ms; R615=12k now pulls to XEM 3.3 V, R616=100k pulls down.\nStartup and brownout remain unverified; keep OFF during power-up.\nJLC C189211 listing conflicts with TI G30 threshold; verify MPN/marking.\n\nXEM target switch: Codex circuit using TI TS3A27518E Rev F Fig.5-2, Table 8-1:\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/ts3a27518e.pdf\nIN1/IN2 high select NO; active-low EN from rotary; 10k pullup. Channels (Howard 1 Nov 2026, for straight PCB routing): TCK=4, TDI=6, TMS=3, TDO=5, VREF=2; channel 1 unused.\nNO2-NO6: ±6 kV IEC contact rating; not a 5 V DC clamp.\nSelection, leakage, power-off and SI need checks.\nXEM JTAG pins: https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8310/expansion-connectors/" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1077 296 0) (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2fec8c0f-d1e9-4c3c-b910-78a021c9738f"))

